        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1+2\\sqrt{2}$, taking the positive root.",
          "worked": "By Pythagoras’ Theorem:\n$$\\begin{align*}\nx^2+(x+3)^2&=(x+4)^2\\\\\n2x^2+6x+9&=x^2+8x+16\\\\\nx^2-2x-7&=0\n\\end{align*}$$\nWith $a=1$, $b=-2$ and $c=-7$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\nx&=\\frac{-(-2)\\pm\\sqrt{(-2)^2-4(1)(-7)}}{2(1)}\\\\\nx&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{32}}{2}\\\\\nx&=1\\pm2\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x$ is a length, reject the negative root. Thus $x=1+2\\sqrt{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q5-hence",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence find the exact perimeter and area using your knowledge of surd laws.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P=10+6\\sqrt{2}$; $A=6+5\\sqrt{2}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\nP&=x+(x+3)+(x+4)\\\\\nP&=3(1+2\\sqrt{2})+7\\\\\nP&=10+6\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe perpendicular sides are $x$ and $x+3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\nA&=\\frac12x(x+3)\\\\\nA&=\\frac12(1+2\\sqrt{2})(4+2\\sqrt{2})\\\\\nA&=\\frac12(12+10\\sqrt{2})\\\\\nA&=6+5\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      }
    ]
  },
